**Note:** This is a simplified version, and you may want to add more details and optimizations depending on your specific use case.

**Recursive Ray Tracing Algorithm (RRT) Pseudocode:**
```python
function traceRay(ray, depth):
  // Initialize reflection and refraction variables
  reflect = false
  refract = false

  // Check if the ray intersects with any objects (e.g., spheres, planes)
  if intersectsObject(ray) then
    // Calculate the intersection point and normal
    intersectionPoint = calculateIntersectionPoint(ray)
    normal = calculateNormal(intersectionPoint)

    // Calculate the material properties (e.g., reflectivity, refraction index)
    materialProperties = getMaterialProperties(intersectionPoint)

    // Calculate the reflection vector
    reflectionVector = calculateReflectionVector(ray, normal)

    // Check if the intersection is reflective
